      "timestamp_minutes": 10.0,
      "type": "reassess",
      "args": {},
      "justification": "High-quality CPR (rate 100-120/min, depth \u22652 inches, full recoil, minimal interruptions) is the cornerstone of cardiac arrest management and must be initiated immediately. Delaying CPR is contraindicated per AHA ACLS guidelines."
    },
    {
      "action_id": "attach_defibrillator_pads",
      "timestamp_minutes": 15.0,
      "type": "reassess",
      "args": {},
      "justification": "MANDATORY action per ACLS protocol. Attaching defibrillator pads is the immediate next step to enable rhythm analysis and potential defibrillation. This must be done before rhythm can be assessed."
    },
    {
      "action_id": "analyze_rhythm",
      "timestamp_minutes": 20.0,
      "type": "reassess",
      "args": {},
      "justification": "After attaching pads, rhythm analysis is essential to differentiate shockable rhythms (VF/pVT) from non-shockable rhythms (asystole/PEA), which determines whether defibrillation or epinephrine is the priority intervention."
    },
    {
